# Clean Architecture & SOLID

## Purpose

Default structural model when the project has no stronger convention documented elsewhere.
**Project-specific layout always wins** over this template.

## Layer Model

```
Presentation → Application → Domain ← Infrastructure
     UI/API handlers    use-cases    entities/rules    DB, HTTP, queues
```

**Dependency rule:** inner layers never import outer layers.

| Layer          | Responsibility                           | Must NOT                   |
| -------------- | ---------------------------------------- | -------------------------- |
| Presentation   | HTTP handlers, UI components, routing    | Business rules, SQL        |
| Application    | Use-cases, orchestration, DTO mapping    | Framework-specific details |
| Domain         | Entities, value objects, domain services | HTTP, ORM, UI              |
| Infrastructure | Repositories, adapters, external APIs    | Business policy            |

## SOLID (Actionable)

- **S** — One reason to change per module/class.
- **O** — Extend via new types/strategies, not by editing stable core.
- **L** — Substitutes must honor contracts (interfaces).
- **I** — Small, focused interfaces; no "god" repositories.
- **D** — Depend on abstractions (ports); inject adapters in composition root.

## Folder Heuristic (adjust to project)

```
src/
  modules/<feature>/
    domain/
    application/
    infrastructure/
    presentation/
  shared/
```

## AI Behavior

- Place new code in the **correct layer**; split files when responsibilities diverge.
- Before proposing a new top-level folder structure: inspect existing layout and justify deviations.
- Prefer **feature modules** over technical silos (`controllers/`, `services/` everywhere) in greenfield work.